      "subject": "Mexico Storm",
      "summary": "Mexico Storm refers to Hurricane Polo, an eastern North Pacific tropical cyclone that developed south of Mexico and intensified rapidly while tracking near the country’s southwestern Pacific coast. As of September 23, 2026, its outer rainbands were affecting coastal areas, creating risks from heavy rain, flooding, mudslides, dangerous surf and tropical-storm-force winds even though the storm’s core was forecast to remain offshore.",
